Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-04-23T20:54:27Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T16:09:49Z","closed_at":"2026-05-18T16:09:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.7 dev, commit 1c8cc9e7e2c9a083cf726e74193d3824fb38cda4\n\n### System information\n\nLinux, Debian 13, KDE Plasma, X11\n\n### Issue description\n\nI compiled a github pull of 4.7 dev earlier today, and was going a bit crazy as it seemed like the editor was randomly re-enabling the \"auto-orthogonal\" toggle, but that wasn't part of it. Turns out when I alt+tab, it doesn't register the alt key has stopped being pressed, until I press it again. So until that happens, the 3D view snaps to 45 degree angles when you orbit the camera.\n\nI can't seem to find any other things that think alt is still held down other than the 3D view, but I haven't tested every nook and cranny.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAlt-tab out of the editor to another window, then go back into it. Try to orbit the 3D view camera and it will snap as if you were still holding alt.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCan be reproduced in blank editor","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscr